// 1-23: every gate has a different idea.
id l1-23
name 1-23 FLOODGATES
tagline every gate has a different idea.
bg city
// RULES: what this room is about, how often each mechanic shows up, how hard each portion is (docs/level-design-rules.md)
main anchor white capacitor
mechanics current:22 pull:2 anchor:14 yank:2 hack:1 capacitor:3 neon:3 white:5
new -
portion 2.5 steps up 3 tall and back down (12 wide)
portion 6.4 hop 5 floating blocks over current (heights 21123)
portion 5.1 hack port opens a gate, 5-wide current beyond
portion 3.5 steps up 4 tall and back down (15 wide)
portion 5.8 neon/white stones nWnW (3 wide, 3 apart) over current
portion 6.5 drive a rail 8 long, swing a 26 gap (mid, ceiling anchors)
portion 5 capacitor gate 18 tiles away
portion 6.5 drive a rail 8 long, swing a 26 gap (mid, high anchors)
portion 6 two pull ports up to the top lane
portion 5.8 neon/white stones nWWW (3 wide, 3 apart) over current
portion 4.7 hop 2 blocks 3 tall and 2 wide over 3-wide current
portion 5 a low ceiling 10 long over a current notch
portion 7.1 capacitor gate 24 tiles away, a block on the way
portion 5.5 a 4-tall plateau 9 wide with a current notch on top
portion 4.8 zip 2 anchors (mid, mid), 8 apart, over current
portion 6.6 capacitor gate 22 tiles away, a block on the way
portion 6.3 zip 4 anchors (ceiling, ceiling, ceiling, high), 8-7-8 apart, over current
portion 6.5 zip 4 anchors (ceiling, high, high, high), 8-8-9 apart, over current
hardness 5.5
map
